# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/spotlight_famous.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event spot_endorsement
# en: Your Face on a Candle
title [d6592c] = 蜡烛上的你
# en: The village chandler wants to sell "{player}'s study candles: they burn all night, like genius". Your face on every label, a crown or two from every box. He's already had the labels painted. They look almost like you.
text [e68ed8] = 村里的蜡烛匠想卖“{player}牌学习蜡烛：通宵长明，如天才一般”。每张标签上都是你的脸，每卖一盒你就能分一两个克朗。标签他已经请人画好了。看上去几乎像你。
# en: A village chandler's shop window full of candles, each with a little painted label of a student's face, the chandler beaming in the doorway.
scene [24c4ba] = 村里一家蜡烛铺的橱窗摆满了蜡烛，每支上都贴着一张画有学生面孔的小标签，蜡烛匠站在门口笑容满面。
# en: Lend your name
opt.left.label [1df9b2] = 借出你的名字
# en: The candles burn all night, as promised, and give off a smell like a wet dog. Half the dormitory sleeps with the windows open. Someone writes "GENIUS" under your painted face, with an arrow, in soot.
opt.left.say.1 [2a7bbf] = 蜡烛如约通宵长明，同时散发出一股湿狗的味道。半个宿舍的人只好开着窗睡觉。有人用烟灰在你那张画出来的脸下面写了“天才”，还画了个箭头。
# en: The candles sell out twice. They're perfectly ordinary candles, but people study by them with great seriousness, and the chandler sends a box up to you every month, with your own face looking back from the label.
opt.left.say.2 [205bc3] = 蜡烛卖断了两次货。它们只是再普通不过的蜡烛，可人们点着它们读书时都郑重其事，蜡烛匠每个月都给你送上来一盒，标签上你自己的脸回望着你。
# en: Turn him down
opt.right.label [b56858] = 拒绝他
# en: You tell him, kindly, that your face isn't for sale. He sighs and paints over the labels. The next week they say "a famous student's study candles", and sell almost as well.
opt.right.say.1 [dbd2a1] = 你和气地告诉他，你的脸不卖。他叹了口气，把标签涂掉了。第二周，标签上写的是“某位名学生的学习蜡烛”，卖得几乎一样好。

@event spot_memoir
# en: As Told To
title [79a8c3] = 口述实录
# en: A man from a city publisher has come all the way up the hill to offer you a sum for your memoir. You won't have to write a word: "Our writer does all that. You just tell her a few stories, and sign." He has a draft title already. It has an exclamation mark.
text [5e77ae] = 一位城里出版社的人一路爬上山来，出一笔钱要买你的回忆录。你一个字都不用写：“我们的写手全包了。你只要给她讲几个故事，然后签字。”他连书名都拟好了。还带着一个感叹号。
# en: A smart stranger in a travelling coat at a refectory table, a contract and a quill laid out in front of a student.
scene [477ef8] = 膳堂的桌边坐着一位穿旅行外套的体面陌生人，一份合同和一支羽毛笔摆在一个学生面前。
# en: Sign
opt.left.label [6340c4] = 签字
# en: The first chapter is printed in the Ledger as a teaser. In it you wrestle a lake serpent, win a duel blindfold and kiss three people on one page. You have done none of these things. The whole castle reads it aloud at breakfast, in voices.
opt.left.say.1 [f0b59d] = 第一章作为预告登在了《纪事报》上。书里你和湖中巨蛇搏斗，蒙着眼睛赢了一场决斗，还在一页之内亲了三个人。这些事你一件都没做过。全城堡的人在早餐时把它大声念出来，还配上了腔调。
# en: The book is short and breathless and only slightly made up. It sells in the city, and copies come back up the hill, where first-years read it under the desks. You sign one, once, and then hide.
opt.left.say.2 [ab0a00] = 这本书篇幅不长，读来令人屏息，只稍微编造了一点。它在城里卖得不错，几本又流回了山上，一年级生把它藏在课桌底下读。你签过一本，就一次，然后就躲起来了。
# en: Decline
opt.right.label [eaef39] = 婉拒
# en: You tell him you're still in the middle of it, and you'd like to find out how it ends first. He laughs, leaves his card, and takes the long way down the hill.
opt.right.say.1 [018928] = 你告诉他你还在故事的中间，想先看看结局如何。他笑了，留下名片，绕远路下了山。

@event spot_impostor
# en: The Other {player}
title [eb5455] = 另一个{player}
# en: The baker asks, very politely, when you're going to settle your account. You haven't got one. It turns out somebody in an academy scarf has been eating very well in the village for a month and signing your name, with a flourish, at the bakery, the tearoom and the Newt.
text [1169cd] = 面包师非常客气地问你，什么时候结清你的账。你根本没有账。原来有人围着学院颜色的围巾，在村里吃香喝辣了一个月，在面包房、茶室和蝾螈酒馆都签了你的名字，还签得龙飞凤舞。
# en: A village bakery counter, a slip of paper pinned up reading "on account", a hooded figure in academy-coloured scarf ducking out of the back door.
scene [591e45] = 村里面包房的柜台上钉着一张写着“记账”的纸条，一个围着学院颜色围巾的兜帽身影正从后门溜出去。
# en: Catch them in the act
opt.left.label [59255a] = 当场抓住对方
# en: You catch the impostor at the bakery on market day, in front of a crowd. The impostor is a thin first-year who hadn't eaten properly in weeks. The crowd looks at you as if you'd kicked a puppy. You pay the account. It doesn't help much.
opt.left.say.1 [db8704] = 赶集那天你在面包房当着一群人的面抓住了冒名者。那是个瘦弱的一年级生，已经好几个星期没好好吃过饭了。人群看你的眼神就像你踢了一只小狗。你结清了账。这没多大用。
# en: You catch the impostor in the act at the Newt: a grinning fourth-year who's done it for a bet. The landlady makes them pay every crown back, and you get a free supper and a story that does the rounds for weeks.
opt.left.say.2 [a3163d] = 你在蝾螈酒馆当场抓住了冒名者：一个咧嘴笑的四年级生，为了打赌才这么干。老板娘让对方一个克朗不少地全还了回来，你得了一顿免费晚餐，还有一个流传了好几个星期的故事。
# en: Pay the bills, and leave a note
opt.right.label [197c5f] = 付清账单，留张字条
# en: You pay what's owed and leave a note with the baker: "If they come back, feed them, and tell them to come and see me." A week later, a thin first-year turns up at your door, and you find them a job at the Newt.
opt.right.say.1 [759c66] = 你付清了欠账，给面包师留了张字条：“如果对方再来，就给饭吃，再让对方来找我。”一个星期后，一个瘦弱的一年级生出现在你门口，你给对方在蝾螈酒馆找了份活。

@event spot_fan_circle
# en: The {player} Society
title [2a546d] = {player}协会
# en: There is a society. It meets on Tuesdays in the disused classroom at the top of the lecture tower. It has a banner, ribbons, minutes and a portrait of you, done in crayon. Its president has written asking whether you would honour them with a visit.
text [af7082] = 有一个协会。每周二在讲堂塔顶那间废弃的教室聚会。它有横幅、缎带、会议记录，还有一幅用蜡笔画的你的肖像。会长写信来问，你是否愿意赏光来访。
# en: A disused classroom with a hand-painted banner, a dozen younger students in matching ribbons sitting in a circle, a portrait of one student propped on a chair.
scene [4ce436] = 一间废弃的教室挂着手绘的横幅，十来个系着同样缎带的年轻学生围坐成一圈，一幅学生的画像靠在一把椅子上。
# en: Visit, and make a fuss of them
opt.left.label [27476c] = 去看看，好好捧捧他们
# en: The society is thrilled, and sets out to honour you properly. The next morning your name is written across the observatory dome in luminous paint, misspelled. The headmistress asks to see you. So does the observatory.
opt.left.say.1 [32618d] = 协会激动万分，决定好好向你致敬。第二天早上，你的名字被人用夜光漆写在了观星台的穹顶上，还拼错了。院长要见你。观星台那边也要。
# en: You visit, sign the minutes, admire the portrait, and answer their questions for an hour. The society is beside itself. You have, from then on, a dozen first-years who would walk into the lake for you, and who very kindly don't.
opt.left.say.2 [f814ff] = 你去了，在会议记录上签了名，夸了那幅肖像，回答了他们一个小时的问题。协会的人高兴得不得了。从那以后，你有了十几个愿意为你跳进湖里的一年级生，而他们很体贴地没有真跳。
# en: Ask them to do something useful
opt.right.label [c974ac] = 请他们做点有用的事
# en: You visit, and suggest that a society in your name might run a study table for first-years who are struggling. They look crestfallen, and then very determined. By spring, the study table is the best thing about Tuesdays.
opt.right.say.1 [5a3650] = 你去了，建议一个以你命名的协会不妨给学得吃力的一年级生办个学习桌。他们先是垂头丧气，接着变得非常坚决。到了春天，那张学习桌成了每周二最好的事。

@event spot_thornwick_challenge
# en: A Challenge From Across the Hills
title [bc6a2f] = 来自山那边的挑战
# en: A Thornwick student has sent a challenge, very publicly, by way of a notice in a red seal on the courtyard board: "We hear Lumenhold's famous {player} is the best you've got. A contest of spells at the boundary stones, at the month's end. Bring a crowd." Half the castle has already promised to come.
text [572c91] = 一个荆木学院的学生大张旗鼓地发来挑战，用一张盖着红色荆木印章的告示钉在庭院的布告板上：“听说流明堡著名的{player}是你们最好的人。月底，界石旁，比一场法术。多带些观众来。”半个城堡的人已经说好要去了。
# en: A pinned notice on the courtyard board with a red Thornwick seal, a crowd of students reading it and turning to look at one student.
scene [ebd32d] = 庭院的布告板上钉着一张盖着红色荆木印章的告示，一群学生读着告示，转头看向一个学生。
# en: Accept
opt.left.label [b26149] = 接受
# en: The contest at the boundary stones lasts four minutes. You win it on the last spell, with the whole of Lumenhold roaring behind you. The Thornwick student shakes your hand, says "next year", and means it.
opt.left.say.1 [803e08] = 界石旁的比试只持续了四分钟。你在最后一个法术上赢了，身后整个流明堡都在欢呼。荆木的学生和你握了握手，说了句“明年见”，而且是认真的。
# en: You lose, fairly and very publicly, to a Thornwick student who is simply better on the day. The walk back up the hill is long and quiet. Thornwick's paper prints the result in very large letters.
opt.left.say.2 [453cf8] = 你输了，输得公平，也输得人尽皆知，对手是个那天就是比你强的荆木学生。回山上的路又长又安静。荆木的校报用非常大的字登出了结果。
# en: Answer with a letter
opt.right.label [fc938e] = 写信回应
# en: You pin a reply under the challenge: "Lumenhold doesn't perform on request. Do come for the Spring Tournament." The castle is a little disappointed, and a little proud. Thornwick's reply, if there is one, never arrives.
opt.right.say.1 [bce8e8] = 你在挑战书下面钉了一张回信：“流明堡不应邀表演。春季锦标赛欢迎光临。”城堡里的人有点失望，也有点自豪。荆木的回信，如果有的话，始终没有到。

@event spot_settle_dispute
# en: Your Word on It
title [102bf0] = 听你一句话
# en: The Duelling Circle and the Skyrace Squad have both booked the flight field for the same Saturday, and it has come close to blows. Somebody suggests they let you decide, since everybody listens to you. Both captains agree. Both are glaring at you, and both are certain you'll pick them.
text [8285a1] = 决斗社和天空竞速队都订了同一个周六的飞行场，差点动起手来。有人提议让你来定，因为大家都听你的。两位队长都同意了。两人都瞪着你，都确信你会选自己。
# en: Two groups of students in different club colours glaring at each other across a courtyard, one student standing between them with a hand raised.
scene [c27127] = 两群穿着不同社团颜色的学生隔着庭院怒目相对，一个学生举着手站在他们中间。
# en: Decide it, there and then
opt.left.label [c326e4] = 当场裁决
# en: You give the field to the Squad, who had booked first. By supper the Circle is telling everyone you were bought, and someone remembers you once had a drink with the Squad's captain. It's nonsense. It sticks for a month.
opt.left.say.1 [97028f] = 你把场地判给了先订的竞速队。到晚饭时，决斗社到处说你被收买了，还有人记起你曾经和竞速队队长喝过一杯。纯属胡说。可这话传了一个月。
# en: You give the field to the Squad, who had booked first, and the Circle the Sunday, with the good side of the hall for practice. Both captains grumble, and both shake on it. People start bringing you their arguments.
opt.left.say.2 [c7e2c0] = 你把场地判给了先订的竞速队，周日给决斗社，外加礼堂好的那一边供他们练习。两位队长都嘟囔了几句，也都握手同意了。人们开始把他们的争执带来找你。
# en: Make them settle it themselves
opt.right.label [8e7b51] = 让他们自己解决
# en: You sit both captains down with a pot of tea and refuse to leave until they've worked it out. It takes three hours and the whole pot. They share the field, half the day each, and claim it was their idea.
opt.right.say.1 [ebec62] = 你让两位队长坐下，泡了一壶茶，说不谈出结果你就不走。这花了三个小时，喝光了整壶茶。他们平分了场地，一人半天，还说这是他们自己的主意。
# en: You sit them down, and they argue for three hours, and in the end neither gets the field, because the groundskeeper has booked it for mowing. Both clubs blame you, slightly, forever.
opt.right.say.2 [a6adfb] = 你让他们坐下，他们吵了三个小时，最后谁也没拿到场地，因为场地管理员早就订好了那天割草。两个社团都怪你，有一点点，永远。

@event spot_charity_auction
# en: An Afternoon With {player}
title [238021] = 与{player}共度一个下午
# en: The infirmary fund is holding an auction, and the top lot, the committee tells you, has to be "an afternoon with {player}": tea, a walk, whatever the winner likes. They think it will raise more than everything else put together. They are probably right.
text [f159c1] = 医务室基金要办一场拍卖会，委员会告诉你，压轴拍品非得是“与{player}共度一个下午”不可：喝茶、散步，随中标者的意。他们认为这一件拍出的钱会比其他所有拍品加起来还多。他们多半是对的。
# en: The Great Hall set out for an auction, a student on a stage holding up a card, a forest of raised hands, an auctioneer with a gavel.
scene [5fedd7] = 大礼堂布置成了拍卖会场，一个学生站在台上举着一张卡片，台下举手如林，拍卖师握着一把木槌。
# en: Agree to be auctioned
opt.left.label [13a1c1] = 同意被拍卖
# en: It raises a fortune. The winner turns out to be the Ledger's worst gossip, who spends the afternoon asking about your love life and prints every word. The infirmary gets new beds. You get a column you'd rather not have read.
opt.left.say.1 [1afe5c] = 拍出了一大笔钱。中标者原来是《纪事报》最爱嚼舌根的人，整个下午都在打听你的感情生活，还把每个字都登了出来。医务室添了新床。你得到了一篇你宁愿没读过的专栏。
# en: It raises a fortune. The winner is an old bookbinder from the village, who has saved for a year and only wants to walk round the lake with somebody famous and tell them about his garden. It's one of the best afternoons you have.
opt.left.say.2 [d36dc1] = 拍出了一大笔钱。中标者是村里一位年迈的装订匠，攒了一年的钱，只想和一个名人绕着湖走一圈，跟对方讲讲自己的花园。那是你度过的最好的下午之一。
# en: Give the fund a donation instead
opt.right.label [a4427f] = 改为向基金捐款
# en: You give the committee what you can, and ask them to auction something more useful than you. They auction the headmistress's old hat, which raises almost as much and is far less trouble.
opt.right.say.1 [66ec74] = 你尽自己所能捐了一笔，请委员会拍卖点比你更有用的东西。他们拍卖了院长的旧帽子，拍出的钱差不多一样多，麻烦却少得多。

@event spot_newt_drink
# en: Whatever You're Having
title [f16c9d] = 照你的来
# en: Whatever you order at the Gilded Newt, half the bar orders next, and the landlady has noticed. She leans over the counter. "Do me a favour, love. Order the elderflower fizz. I've forty bottles of it in the cellar and nobody's touched one since midsummer. There's a cut in it for you." The whole bar is waiting to see what you'll have.
text [594688] = 你在镀金蝾螈酒馆点什么，半个酒馆的人就跟着点什么，老板娘早注意到了。她从柜台后探过身来。“帮个忙，亲爱的。点一杯接骨木花汽酒吧。我地窖里有四十瓶，从仲夏到现在一瓶都没人碰过。少不了你的分成。”整个酒馆都在等着看你点什么。
# en: A tavern bar, a landlady leaning over the counter with a dusty bottle of pale fizz, the whole room turned to watch one student order.
scene [dcd7a2] = 酒馆吧台边，老板娘探身越过柜台，手里拿着一瓶落满灰的淡色汽酒，满屋子的人都转过头来看一个学生点单。
# en: "One elderflower fizz, please."
opt.left.label [153ff7] = “来一杯接骨木花汽酒。”
# en: The fizz has been in the cellar since midsummer for a reason. Half the bar orders one after you, and half the bar spends the rest of the evening outside. The landlady gives you your cut anyway. By morning everyone knows whose idea it was.
opt.left.say.1 [dab963] = 那瓶汽酒从仲夏起就待在地窖里，是有原因的。半个酒馆的人跟着你点了一杯，然后半个酒馆的人整晚都待在外面。老板娘照样给了你分成。到第二天早上，人人都知道这是谁的主意了。
# en: You raise a glass of fizz to the bar, and the bar raises forty back. It is far too sweet. For the rest of the term it's what people drink at the Newt, and every few weeks the landlady presses a small purse of coppers into your hand.
opt.left.say.2 [618a91] = 你举起一杯汽酒向整个酒馆致意，酒馆里举起四十杯回敬你。它甜得过分。这个学期剩下的日子里，大家在蝾螈酒馆都喝这个，每隔几个星期，老板娘就往你手里塞一小袋铜板。
# en: Order what you always have
opt.right.label [3355fd] = 照常点你平时喝的
# en: You order your usual. So does half the bar. The landlady sighs, says "Traitor" quite fondly, and goes down to the cellar for more of it. The fizz stays where it is.
opt.right.say.1 [bbd26a] = 你点了你平时喝的。半个酒馆的人也点了一样的。老板娘叹了口气，相当亲昵地骂了声“叛徒”，下到地窖里去多拿几瓶。那些汽酒原封不动。

@event spot_lecture_crowds
# en: Standing Room Only
title [eaed8a] = 只剩站票
# en: Your lectures have filled up. Not with people who take the course: with people who want to sit near you. They sit in the aisles. They sit on the windowsills. After class, the lecturer asks you to stay behind, and says, without warmth, "This is a lecture, not a menagerie. Do something about it."
text [d2af75] = 你的课坐满了人。不是选这门课的人：是想坐在你附近的人。他们坐在过道里。他们坐在窗台上。下课后，讲师让你留下，毫无暖意地说：“这是讲课，不是动物园。想想办法。”
# en: A lecture hall crammed with students sitting in the aisles and on the windowsills, a lecturer at the front glaring over spectacles at one student in the third row.
scene [e8c2f7] = 阶梯教室里挤满了学生，过道和窗台上都坐着人，讲台上的讲师从眼镜上方瞪着第三排的一个学生。
# en: Hold a question time after class
opt.left.label [7f0d3c] = 课后设个答疑时间
# en: You offer a half-hour of questions after class, for anyone. The first question is about your love life. The second is about your hair. The lecturer comes back for a book, sees the circus, and gives you an essay to write on decorum.
opt.left.say.1 [8726be] = 你在课后开了半小时答疑，谁都可以来。第一个问题是关于你的感情生活。第二个是关于你的头发。讲师回来拿书，看见这副马戏团的场面，罚你写一篇关于礼仪的论文。
# en: You offer a half-hour of questions after class, and to your surprise most of them are about the lecture. By the end of the month you know the course better than ever, and the aisles are clear: people come to your half-hour instead.
opt.left.say.2 [966afa] = 你在课后开了半小时答疑，出乎意料的是，大部分问题都是关于这门课的。到月底，你对这门课比以往任何时候都熟，过道也空了：人们改来参加你的半小时。
# en: Sit at the back, in a hood
opt.right.label [49051c] = 坐到后排，戴上兜帽
# en: You sit at the back with your hood up, take careful notes and leave by the side door. The crowds drift away to look at something else. The lecturer gives you, at the end of term, the very smallest nod.
opt.right.say.1 [5569b9] = 你戴着兜帽坐在后排，认真记笔记，从侧门离开。人群渐渐散去，去看别的热闹了。学期末，讲师朝你点了点头，幅度小得不能再小。

@event spot_luck_sleeve
# en: For Luck
title [83cd21] = 图个好运
# en: Somebody has decided that touching your sleeve before an exam brings luck. The queue outside the exam hall reaches out as you pass, one after another, very solemnly. A first-year asks if you'd mind breathing on their quill.
text [1e9490] = 有人认定考试前摸一摸你的袖子能带来好运。考场外排队的人在你经过时一个接一个地伸出手，神情非常庄重。一个一年级生问你介不介意朝那支羽毛笔哈口气。
# en: A corridor outside an exam hall, a nervous queue of students each reaching out to touch one student's sleeve as they pass.
scene [4a603b] = 考场外的走廊里，一排紧张的学生在一个学生经过时，一个接一个地伸手去碰这个学生的袖子。
# en: Bless them all, grandly
opt.left.label [45c92a] = 隆重地为所有人祝福
# en: You bless every quill and sleeve with great ceremony. When the results come out, a first-year who failed writes to the Ledger to say that your luck "is a fraud, and so are you". The letter is printed. Several people agree with it loudly.
opt.left.say.1 [2332c7] = 你郑重其事地为每一支羽毛笔、每一只袖子祝了福。成绩出来后，一个没考过的一年级生写信给《纪事报》，说你的好运“是个骗局，你也是”。信登了出来。好几个人大声表示赞同。
# en: You bless every quill with great ceremony, and the queue goes in laughing, which is better for them than any luck. Afterwards three of them find you to say they passed. You don't point out that most people do.
opt.left.say.2 [6f0716] = 你郑重其事地为每一支羽毛笔祝了福，排队的人笑着走进考场，这比任何好运都对他们更有用。事后有三个人来找你，说他们考过了。你没有指出大多数人都会考过。
# en: Tell them to trust their work
opt.right.label [ba0698] = 让他们相信自己的努力
# en: You tell the queue, kindly, that your sleeve has never passed an exam, and that they've done the work. Some of them look let down. One of them, a first-year with very cold hands, says thank you and goes in steadier.
opt.right.say.1 [a9e9c3] = 你和气地告诉排队的人，你的袖子从没考过一场试，而他们已经下过功夫了。有些人显得有点失望。其中一个手冰凉的一年级生道了声谢，走进去时稳当了些。

@event spot_routine_known
# en: Where to Find {player}
title [c04713] = 去哪儿找{player}
# en: Someone has printed your whole week in a gossip sheet: which mornings you're in the library, where you sit for lunch, which way you walk back. By Tuesday there's a crowd on the library steps at nine o'clock, waiting, and the librarians are not pleased.
text [b942ab] = 有人把你一整周的行程登在了一份八卦小报上：哪几个早上你在图书馆，午饭坐在哪儿，回去走哪条路。到了周二，九点钟的图书馆台阶上已经聚了一群人在等，图书管理员们很不高兴。
# en: A gossip sheet pinned to a board with a timetable printed on it, a crowd gathering on the library steps, a student watching from a corner with books held to their chest.
scene [192163] = 布告板上钉着一份印着时间表的八卦小报，一群人聚在图书馆台阶上，一个学生把书抱在胸前，从角落里看着。
# en: Hold court on the steps
opt.left.label [dfa614] = 在台阶上接见众人
# en: You stop on the steps and chat, and the crowd grows, and grows, until it blocks the library door. The librarians ban you, very politely, for a week. The crowd moves on to the Newt. You fall behind on everything.
opt.left.say.1 [4a9974] = 你在台阶上停下来聊天，人越聚越多，直到堵住了图书馆的门。图书管理员们非常客气地禁止你入馆一周。人群转移到了蝾螈酒馆。你什么都落下了。
# en: You stop on the steps each morning for ten minutes, answer whatever people ask, and then go inside. The crowd shrinks to a friendly handful who bring you tea. The librarians decide they can live with it.
opt.left.say.2 [0d28da] = 你每天早上在台阶上停留十分钟，有问必答，然后进去。人群渐渐缩成一小撮友好的人，还给你带茶。图书管理员们觉得这还能忍。
# en: Change everything
opt.right.label [c6188a] = 全部改掉
# en: You change your mornings, your lunch table, your way back. It takes a week to get it right and you keep getting lost. But you find a window seat in a disused stair where nobody comes, and you work better there than you have all year.
opt.right.say.1 [e3f522] = 你改了早上的安排、午饭的桌子、回去的路。花了一个星期才调整好，你还总是迷路。不过你找到了一处没人去的废弃楼梯间的窗台，在那儿学习的效率比这一年里任何时候都高。

@event spot_guest_flyer
# en: A Guest Lap
title [1381e1] = 表演一圈
# en: The Skyrace Squad wants you to fly a guest lap at the season's opening race: just once round the course, before the real race starts, for the crowd. "It'll double the gate," the captain says. "Nobody's going to watch you race. They'll just watch you fly." The course goes out over the lake.
text [1e8cc3] = 天空竞速队想请你在赛季揭幕赛上飞一圈表演：在正式比赛开始前，绕赛道飞一圈就好，给观众看。“门票能翻倍，”队长说，“没人要看你比赛。他们只想看你飞。”赛道要飞越湖面。
# en: A flight field ringed by a packed crowd, banners snapping, one student on a borrowed broom at the starting line, the lake glittering beyond.
scene [37fe5f] = 飞行场四周挤满了观众，旗帜猎猎作响，一个学生骑着借来的飞帚停在起跑线上，远处的湖面波光粼粼。
# en: Fly it
opt.left.label [21fb6b] = 飞
# en: You fly the lap clean and a little faster than you should, and the crowd stands up to roar as you come round the last marker. The Squad captain is grinning. For the rest of the season, small children run about the field with brooms, being you.
opt.left.say.1 [3bd6c9] = 你干净利落地飞完了一圈，还稍微快了点，绕过最后一个标志时观众站起来欢呼。竞速队队长咧着嘴笑。那个赛季剩下的日子里，小孩子们骑着扫帚在场上跑来跑去，扮演你。
# en: You fly it beautifully, right up to the last marker over the lake, where you misjudge the wind and go into the water in front of the whole academy. The crowd's gasp is louder than any cheer. Your own laughter, when you surface, saves a little of it.
opt.left.say.2 [ce5c4c] = 你飞得很漂亮，一直到湖面上的最后一个标志，你算错了风向，当着整个学院的面掉进了水里。观众的惊呼声比任何欢呼都响。你浮出水面时自己的笑声，多少挽回了一点。
# en: Present the trophy instead
opt.right.label [018ab9] = 改为颁奖
# en: You stay on the ground and present the trophy at the end, which takes a speech and no risk at all. The crowd is perfectly happy. The captain looks at your boots, and then the sky, and doesn't say anything.
opt.right.say.1 [801db5] = 你留在地面上，在最后颁发奖杯，只需讲几句话，毫无风险。观众完全满意。队长看了看你的靴子，又看了看天空，什么也没说。

@event spot_petition
# en: Your Name at the Top
title [a1bf06] = 你的名字签在最上面
# en: A petition is going round to keep the library open all night in exam weeks. It has a hundred and twelve names and a blank line at the top, which the second-year carrying it would like you to fill. "If your name's on it, they'll have to listen." The scroll goes on for quite a long way below the main request.
text [04041a] = 一份请愿书正在传阅，要求考试周图书馆通宵开放。上面已经有一百一十二个名字，最上面留着一行空白，拿着它的二年级生希望你来填。“只要你的名字在上面，他们就不得不听。”主要诉求下面，卷轴还拖得相当长。
# en: A student holding out a long scroll petition with dozens of signatures, a quill in the other hand, the top line left blank.
scene [4c3d2b] = 一个学生一手举着长长的请愿卷轴，上面有几十个签名，另一只手拿着羽毛笔，最上面一行空着。
# en: Sign at the top
opt.left.label [64397d] = 签在最上面
# en: The headmistress reads it out at supper, all of it, including clause nine (puddings twice a day) and clause twelve (the abolition of Thursdays), "proposed by {player}". The hall laughs for a full minute. The library stays shut.
opt.left.say.1 [a12d08] = 院长在晚餐时把它从头到尾念了出来，包括第九条（一天两顿布丁）和第十二条（废除星期四），“由{player}提议”。整个大厅笑了足足一分钟。图书馆照旧关门。
# en: The library stays open all night in exam weeks. The petition is framed and hung by the door, with your name at the top, and in the small hours there are students at every desk, and someone always brings you a cup of tea.
opt.left.say.2 [51c881] = 考试周图书馆通宵开放了。请愿书被装进画框挂在门边，你的名字在最上面，深夜里每张桌子边都坐着学生，总有人给你端来一杯茶。
# en: Read it all first
opt.right.label [4c4f9b] = 先从头读一遍
# en: You read it all, which takes a while. Clause nine asks for puddings twice a day. Clause twelve abolishes Thursdays. You hand it back with a note on how to make it shorter. The second-year looks very let down, and then, the next week, comes back with one clause, which you sign.
opt.right.say.1 [a1269c] = 你从头到尾读了一遍，花了不少时间。第九条要求一天两顿布丁。第十二条要废除星期四。你把它还了回去，附了张字条，教对方怎么改短。那个二年级生显得很失望，然后，第二周，拿着只剩一条的请愿书回来了，你签了。

@event spot_party_host
# en: The Party, If You Come
title [5927e0] = 只要你来
# en: A second-year is throwing a party in the old music room on Saturday, and says frankly that it'll either be the party of the term or a sad evening with twelve people and a fiddle, depending entirely on whether you come. Everybody knows already that you've been asked. Everybody is waiting to see.
text [2a8396] = 一个二年级生周六要在旧音乐室开派对，坦白说，这场派对要么是本学期最棒的，要么是十二个人加一把小提琴的冷清夜晚，全看你来不来。大家都已经知道你被邀请了。大家都在等着看。
# en: A student at a dormitory door holding out a handwritten invitation, behind them a room strung with lanterns and stacked with crates.
scene [0a5669] = 一个学生站在宿舍门口递出一张手写的请柬，身后的房间里挂着灯笼，堆着板条箱。
# en: Go
opt.left.label [d0c56b] = 去
# en: Everyone comes. Everyone. At one o'clock the prefects come too, and the report that goes to the headmistress names one guest by name, at the top. You spend a week of evenings in detention polishing the trophy cabinet, and the castle talks about it for a month.
opt.left.say.1 [9684f2] = 大家都来了。所有人。凌晨一点，级长们也来了，交给院长的报告上，最上面点名写着一位客人的名字。你花了一个星期的晚上被关禁闭擦奖杯柜，城堡里议论了一个月。
# en: It's the party of the term. You dance badly, talk to everyone, and leave before it gets out of hand. On Monday a dozen people you'd never met say hello to you in the corridors, and the second-year is a legend.
opt.left.say.2 [b0eb4b] = 那是本学期最棒的派对。你跳舞跳得很差，和每个人都聊了天，在场面失控之前离开了。周一，十几个你从没见过的人在走廊里跟你打招呼，那个二年级生成了传奇。
# en: Stay in, and wish them well
opt.right.label [4c9d81] = 待在宿舍，祝他们玩得开心
# en: You send a note saying you can't, and a cake. The party is small and very nice, and the twelve people and the fiddle have a lovely time. The second-year sends back a slice.
opt.right.say.1 [026bd9] = 你写了张便条说去不了，还送去一个蛋糕。派对规模不大，非常愉快，那十二个人和那把小提琴玩得很开心。那个二年级生给你送回来一块蛋糕。

@event spot_ball_opening
# en: The First Dance
title [e47601] = 第一支舞
# en: The Midwinter Ball committee has asked you to open the Ball: the first dance, alone on the floor, in front of the whole school, before anybody else may step out. {bonds(partner) > 0: Your partner has gone very pale and is pretending not to have heard.|You'd need to choose someone, and everyone knows it.}
text [5d5899] = 仲冬舞会委员会请你为舞会开场：第一支舞，独自在舞池里，当着全校的面，在你跳之前谁都不能下场。{bonds(partner) > 0: 你的伴侣脸色煞白，正假装没听见。|你得选一个人，大家都知道。}
# en: The Great Hall turned to ice and starlight, an empty dance floor ringed by the whole school, one couple stepping out alone into the middle.
scene [0fb66d] = 大礼堂化作冰与星光，空荡荡的舞池四周围着全校师生，一对舞伴独自走向中央。
# en: Open the Ball
opt.left.label [157b5b] = 为舞会开场
# en: The music starts and, for once, your feet know what to do. You turn once round the whole floor under the floating candles, and when the music ends, the hall applauds before it remembers to dance. People talk about it till spring.
opt.left.say.1 [839283] = 音乐响起，难得一次你的脚知道该怎么走。你在漂浮的蜡烛下绕着整个舞池转了一圈，音乐结束时，大厅先鼓起了掌，才想起来该跳舞了。人们一直谈论到春天。
# en: You start well. Then the ice-floor, the candles and the whole school watching all happen at once, and you go down in a heap at the exact centre of the hall. You get up and finish the dance. The hall cheers more for that than it would have for the steps.
opt.left.say.2 [b31d92] = 你开头很好。然后冰面、蜡烛和全校的目光一下子同时袭来，你在大厅正中央摔成了一团。你爬起来跳完了这支舞。大厅为此欢呼得比为舞步欢呼得还响。
# en: Let someone else open it
opt.right.label [a69926] = 让别人开场
# en: You thank the committee and suggest the two first-years who've been practising for weeks in the boathouse. They open the Ball, nervously and beautifully. You dance later, in the crowd, where nobody's watching, and enjoy every minute.
opt.right.say.1 [63a024] = 你谢过委员会，推荐了那两个在船屋里练了好几个星期的一年级生。他们为舞会开了场，紧张而优美。你后来在人群中跳舞，没人看着，每一分钟都很享受。

@event spot_stable_name
# en: A Name for the Foal
title [9cc0cb] = 给小马起个名字
# en: A winged foal was born at the Familiar Stables last night, and Professor Brask, who claims to have no opinion on the matter, says the first-years will only stop arguing about its name if you choose it. She hands you a slate. The foal looks at you and sneezes.
text [18e7d7] = 昨夜魔宠马厩里生了一匹带翅膀的小马驹，布拉斯克教授声称自己对此毫无意见，却说只有你来起名，一年级生们才会停止争吵。她递给你一块石板。小马驹看着你，打了个喷嚏。
# en: A stable stall with a gangly winged foal tottering on long legs, a professor in a leather apron holding out a slate and chalk to a student.
scene [2543b5] = 马厩隔间里，一匹瘦长的带翅小马驹摇摇晃晃地站在细长的腿上，一位系着皮围裙的教授把石板和粉笔递给一个学生。
# en: Give it a grand name
opt.left.label [1489cb] = 起个气派的名字
# en: You chalk up something grand and ancient and very hard to spell. The first-years approve. The foal grows into it slowly, and in the meantime everybody calls it something else, behind Brask's back, that you suspect is ruder.
opt.left.say.1 [3fcfdd] = 你用粉笔写了一个气派、古老、非常难拼的名字。一年级生们很满意。小马驹慢慢地才配得上这个名字，在此期间，大家背着布拉斯克管它叫别的名字，你怀疑那个更不雅。
# en: Let the first-years vote
opt.right.label [8b1b50] = 让一年级生投票
# en: You hand the slate back and say the first-years should vote. They vote for "Biscuit". Brask writes it in the stable book with the face of a woman enduring something, and the foal, as it turns out, loves it.
opt.right.say.1 [4dfde0] = 你把石板递了回去，说该让一年级生投票。他们投了“饼干”。布拉斯克把它写进马厩的登记簿，脸上是一副忍耐着什么的女人的表情，而事实证明，小马驹很喜欢这个名字。

@event spot_friend_strain
# en: Just {player}'s Friend
title [f98f14] = 只是“{player}的朋友”
# en: {f} sits down beside you on the step and says, without looking at you, "Someone called me '{player}'s friend' today. Not my name. Just that. It's the fourth time this week." {They} laugh{s}, but not much. "I don't mind. I just wanted you to know."
text [8098fb] = {f}在你旁边的台阶上坐下，没有看你，说：“今天有人叫我‘{player}的朋友’。不是我的名字。就这么叫。这个星期已经是第四次了。”{They}笑了笑，但笑得不多。“我不介意。我只是想让你知道。”
# en: Two students sitting on a cold stone step outside the castle at dusk, one with their hands in their pockets, the other turned toward them.
scene [15f9dc] = 黄昏时分，两个学生坐在城堡外冰冷的石阶上，一个双手插在口袋里，另一个侧身朝着对方。
# en: Make time for {f}, away from it all
opt.left.label [1b3f9f] = 抽出时间陪{f}，远离这一切
# en: You start taking {f} to the places no one goes: the boathouse at dusk, the end of the orchard. You let the invitations wait. One evening {f} says something so funny you fall off a jetty, and nobody else is there to see it, and that's the point.
opt.left.say.1 [df4ef2] = 你开始带{f}去没人去的地方：黄昏时的船屋，果园的尽头。你让那些邀请等着。一天傍晚，{f}说了句好笑得让你从栈桥上摔下去的话，而旁边没有别人看见，这正是重点。
# en: Bring {f} into the spotlight with you
opt.right.label [f1d697] = 把{f}也带进聚光灯下
# en: You start bringing {f} everywhere with you, and making sure people hear {f.their} name. After a month, people in corridors start saying "{f} and {player}", in that order. {f} pretends not to notice, and is pleased.
opt.right.say.1 [b56e99] = 你开始走到哪儿都带着{f}，确保大家听到{f.their}名字。一个月后，走廊里的人开始说“{f}和{player}”，按这个顺序。{f}假装没注意到，心里很高兴。
# en: You bring {f} everywhere, and introduce {f.them} to everyone, and {f} goes quieter and quieter. "I didn't want to be famous," {f} says at last. "I wanted you to notice." It takes a while to put right.
opt.right.say.2 [dc1db0] = 你走到哪儿都带着{f}，把{f.them}介绍给每一个人，而{f}变得越来越沉默。“我不想出名，”{f}终于说，“我想让你注意到我。”这花了好一阵子才弥补过来。
